    林德昌: "Lin Dechang",
    林甫: "Lin Fu",
    "林老师：\n\n多谢您百忙之中来信问候。我近来一切皆好，虽不能出海远游，但仍能借着整理货品的机会，窥见远方的故事，实属幸运。您此次带回的几件海国饰品十分有趣，我定会仔细品鉴，为它们寻到合适的买家。\n\n家母近来病况依旧未有好转，我那一双儿女又尚且年幼，我实在不忍留妻子一人操持家中诸务，因此这回恐怕也不能与您同去了。我在商队时，您对我多有提携，在我离开后还数度相邀，感激之余也实在惭愧。只愿您此行一切顺利，旅途中多有奇遇。\n\n此外，我另有一事相求：若您此行恰巧经由海伯利亚的冰湖城，请代我问候一位叫做杰西卡的有龙氏姑娘，她与家妹年纪相仿，如今应是桃李年华。前次我随商队停驻冰湖城时，曾与这位小友结缘，临行时也颇为不舍。本想着总有机会再见，只可惜这一别便是数载。若您能代我送些礼物给她以表歉意，便再好不过了。\n\n恭祝康安\n\n嘉言": "Mr Lin,\n\nThank you for your letter, especially amidst your many responsibilities. I am keeping well. Though I can no longer journey by sea, the work of handling goods still grants me faint glimpses of distant tales — a small comfort, but a comfort nonetheless. The ornaments you brought back from Luca are most intriguing. I shall examine them carefully and seek out suitable buyers.\n\nMy mother's condition has shown no improvement, and my two children are still very young. I cannot, in good conscience, leave the household entirely in my wife's care, and so I must once again decline your generous invitation. During my years with the caravan, you offered me much guidance; even after I left, you continued to welcome me back with the same kindness. I remain deeply grateful — and cannot help feeling a measure of shame for having disappointed you so often. May your journey be smooth, and may fortune grant you auspicious encounters along the way.\n\nI have one further request: if your route happens to pass through Icelake in Hyperborea, please convey my regards to a young Loongscion woman named Jessica. She is about my younger sister's age, and should now be in her finest years. We became acquainted when our caravan last visited the city, and our parting was not an easy one. I had hoped we might meet again before long, yet the years have slipped quietly by. If you would be willing to deliver a few small gifts to her as an apology, I would be most grateful.\n \n With my warmest wishes for your health and peace,\n Jiayan",
