    柳明正: "Liu Mingzheng",
    柳色如故: "As Always",
    "六、雪鸮谣曲 下\n\n雪鸮悲泣 雪鸮啼鸣\n\n雪鸮九度回旋于夜空\n\n雪鸮想要逃离这混乱\n\n可这恶魔是何等狡诈\n\n岂止是这失神的飞鸟\n\n即便是那曾击败伪神的迪斯·盖雷亚\n\n也认定遭到命运的嘲弄\n\n将迎来未曾料得的终结\n\n而唯有一人在卡戎的重重围困中开辟生路\n\n那便是因为因欺瞒而盛怒的索拉努斯·盖雷亚\n\n他愤怒 以燃火的烛台当作长枪熔穿敌人皮甲\n\n他不甘 以盛酒的银杯当作重锤击碎恶徒头盔\n\n他身前的卡戎尽皆倒下\n\n他身后是一条血肉道路\n\n那来此的门扉是他叩开\n\n同样他也定要安然离去\n\n于是迪斯·盖雷亚紧随其后\n\n仿佛从贪食的恶魔的食管中爬出\n\n正当他庆幸旗帜免于被雪水浸没\n\n索拉努斯却耗尽最后气力\n\n恶魔追及了英雄挥下刀刃\n\n那高贵头颅迸出一道白焰\n\n冰川倾倒 鲜血涌泉 凝成粒粒玛瑙\n\n索拉努斯·盖雷亚 迪斯一世唯一的弟兄 就此陨落\n\n大迁徙开始那日他便誓与死亡结伴\n\n然而无人料得命运竟在这一日狞笑\n\n而那试图觅食的雪鸮\n\n亦被卑污的箭支射穿\n\n在血水中失去了气息\n\n痛哉 索拉努斯 呼唤和平的英雄 \n\n他未能见证海伯利亚帝国的建立\n\n但却是帝国的最初的英雄": "Ⅵ. The Snow-Owl's Ballad, Canto Ⅲ\n \n The snow-owl wept, the snow-owl cried,\n \n Nine times it wheeled through the nighted sky.\n \n It longed to flee the tumult —\n \n Yet cunning are the demons,\n \n Who beguile not only the bewildered bird.\n \n Even Dis Galea, who once struck down a false god,\n \n Deemed himself scorned by Fate,\n \n Doomed to an end unimagined.\n \n Only one carved a path through the tightening snare of the Charon:\n \n Soranus Galea, blazing with wrath at deceit.\n \n In fury he cast a burning candelabrum as a spear, piercing the armour of his foes.\n \n In defiance he swung a brimming silver goblet as a hammer, shattering the helms of the wicked.\n \n Before him, the Charon fell in heaps;\n \n Behind him, stretched a road of blood and flesh.\n \n It was he who had once knocked upon that door,\n \n And so he swore he would depart in whole.\n \n Dis Galea followed close behind,\n \n As though clawing free from a demon's ravenous maw.\n \n He rejoiced that his banner yet stood, unswallowed by the snow.\n \n But Soranus had spent his final strength.\n \n The demons overtook him, their blades came down,\n \n And from that noble brow there burst a white flame.\n \n The glacier crumbled, blood welled forth, hardening into stones of crimson agate.\n \n So fell Soranus Galea, sole brother of Dis Ⅰ.\n \n On the day the Great Migration began, he had sworn to march hand in hand with Death.\n \n Yet none foresaw that Fate would on this day bare its fangs in laughter.\n \n And the snow-owl, too, seeking its feast,\n \n Was struck by an accursed arrow,\n \n Its breath lost amid the bloodied waters.\n \n Alas! Soranus — hero who called for peace...\n \n He never lived to behold the birth of the Hyperborean Empire,\n \n Yet he became its first and truest hero.",
    六面骰: "Dice of Fate",
    "六月四日\n申请人：王权\n理由：我认为豆花甜的好吃，但张负认为咸的好吃，只能比试一番，一决胜负！\n\n六月二十八日\n申请人：徐鸿\n理由：想要实验新的爆炸机关，演武场较为空旷，比较合适。\n\n七月十五日\n申请人：苏乙\n理由：陆野和裴景想要练习弓弩，特请我来监督他们。\n\n七月十六日\n申请人：苏乙\n理由：理由同昨日（孩子们真是有出息了！）\n\n八月六日\n申请人：唐叔\n理由：新的战用扩音仪做好了，想要请大家在演武场轮番献唱一曲进行实验。\n\n八月二十日\n申请人：唐叔\n理由：朱朴练武过度伤了腿脚，今日想试验一下给他设计的辅助支架，记录一些数据。\n": "4 June\nFiled by: Wang Quan\nReason: I say sweet tofu pudding is best. Zhang Fu swears by the savoury kind. Only one way to settle it — a match!\n\n28 June\nFiled by: Xu Hong\nReason: I want to test a new explosive prototype. The yard is open enough for it.\n\n15 July\nFiled by: Su Yi\nReason: Lu Ye and Pei Jing want to practise with crossbows. I've been asked to keep an eye on them.\n\n16 July\nFiled by: Su Yi\nReason: Same as yesterday (the kids are really coming along!).\n\n6 August\nFiled by: Uncle Tang\nReason: Finished a new battlefield loudhailer. Need everyone to take turns singing in the yard for a sound test.\n\n20 August\nFiled by: Uncle Tang\nReason: Zhu Pu overtrained and hurt his leg. Want to test the support brace I made for him and log a few measurements.",
