    舞会人偶: "Courtly Marionette",
    "舞会是献给仲夏夜的问候。": "A ball to greet the midsummer night.",
    舞台演绎: "On Stage",
    舞者: " Dancer",
    "舞者不断旋转，舞会永不落幕。": "The dancer spins unceasingly, and the ball never fades.",
    "勿需月老多催，一根红线牵喜，红轿子驻门前。休管那芳生肯不肯，衣裳披，盖头紧，上轿便成了鸳鸯喜事，千千手，推着走，新郎官眼迷心乱，值当是梦里见玄女。\n\n（外等急应下）\n（副净喜介）妙妙！好事连连，当浮三大白！\n（末）天色已晚，佳人在侯，我且告辞罢！\n（净）差矣，八珍楼内日饮百榼，未尝见醉，今何以忸怩至此，倒叫人看了笑话！\n（末）今时不同往日，兄勿恼。\n（起打恭介）\n（净笑介）可笑我错认了铮铮汉子，原是个酒桌前缩头藏颈的小人！\n（净）罢，罢！他既回避，倒也不必为己甚之行。\n（末惊介）何出此言？多年情深，却因这盏中汤便生了嫌隙？\n（净）教你还记着兄弟情深，你即成亲，八方道贺，为何却一碗不愿饮？\n（众声介）是也是也！\n（净）谈何情谊！是何兄弟！\n（众声介）是也是也！\n（末叹介）榴花红似火，何如艾叶烟。也罢。\n（末高呼介）今日当舍命陪君子，诸位公，请了！\n（众饮酒介）\n\n小楼才生婉转月，奈何明月照沟渠，空梳拢，怀抱琵琶向阿谁。": "No need for the Moon Matchmaker to meddle. One red thread binds the romance. The crimson bridal sedan chair halts at the gate. Whether she wills it or no — gown on, veil down — once she mounts, the union is sealed. A hundred hands bear it onwards. The bridegroom reels, heart unmoored, as though he had glimpsed a heavenly maiden in a dream.\n\n(Offstage, a hurried reply.)\nJing (beaming): Splendid! Good luck upon good luck — three cups for that!\nMo: It's late. My lady is waiting. I'll be taking my leave.\nJing: Nonsense! You've drained more cups than I can count at the Bazhen Pavilion and never once been drunk. And now you're baulking at a single cup? You'll be the laughingstock!\nMo: Things aren't what they were. Don't take it amiss, brother.\n(Mo bows with clasped hands.)\nJing (laughing): Ha! And here I thought you were a man of mettle — turns out you go to ground the moment wine's poured.\nJing: Fine, fine. If he's that set on ducking out, no need to push it.\nMo (startled): Why would you say that? All these years of brotherhood, and you'd throw it away over one cup of wine?\nJing: Brotherhood? If that means anything to you — today's your wedding day, everyone's here to toast you. And you won't drink a single cup with us?\nAll: Hear, hear!\nJing: Some loyalty. Some brother.\nAll: Hear, hear!\nMo (sighing): Pomegranate blazes red as fire... and still, it cannot match the bitter smoke of mugwort... Ah, well.\nMo (raising his voice): Today I'll drink with you if it kills me. Gentlemen — your health!\n(All drink.)\n\nA crescent moon crests the little tower, yet its tender light falls only into the gutter. Hair dressed in vain, pipa in hand... whose ear awaits her song?",
